格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"在 Termux(Android)上运行 DeepSeek Harness(dsh)。Run DeepSeek Harness(dsh) on Termux (Android).","id":"gh:1341111520","install_available":false,"language":"Shell","name":"dsh-termux","slug":"ErEbusE/dsh-termux","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","termux"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"在 Termux(Android)上运行 DeepSeek Harness(dsh)。Run DeepSeek Harness(dsh) on Termux (Android)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-termux"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Run DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) on Termux (Android), no root required."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Why this approach"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The usual ways to run a glibc Node app on Android are recompiling everything against Termux's own (b"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ionic) Node, or a proot/glibc chroot. Recompiling forks dsh's entire native dependency chain into a "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"second build you must maintain forever; a chroot adds a translation layer whose file semantics and a"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"ctivity launches still do not match Android's rules. dsh-termux instead ships the **official** Node."},{"id":"p6s5","text":"js linux-arm64 binary — the exact build npm's prebuilt modules were compiled for — on Termux's own g"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"libc runtime, so upstream dsh and its dependencies run unmodified and nothing is ever compiled on-de"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"vice. Only a small patch set adapts the Android-specific problems that remain (SELinux link policy, "},{"id":"p6s8","text":"intent-based browser handoff, Landlock tmpdir grants, cross-site session cookies), and the bundled u"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"pdater re-verifies it on every run; the complete index is PATCHES.md."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> Only **arm64** devices are supported (nearly all modern Android phones are arm64)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Option A: install from a GitHub release"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The installer downloads the newest runtime release, unpacks it and wires up the `dsh` command. Each "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"release bundles the dsh `latest` snapshot taken at release time — the exact version is in the releas"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"e tag. To pin one release, prefix `DSH_RELEASE=<tag>` (tags are `dsh-<bundled dsh>-<project version>"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"`, e.g. `dsh-0.1.1-rc.2-1.0.1`)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### Option B: clone this repo and install locally"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Option B resolves dsh from npm at install time (whatever is published right then); Option A ships th"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"e release-time snapshot. Both end up with the same layout and the same bundled updater."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Verify"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`dsh web` prints `http://127.0.0.1:3080` and opens it in your phone's browser — keep Termux in the *"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"*foreground** while starting it (Android 10+ silently drops background activity launches); the `dsh`"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" command behaves exactly like the official upstream CLI, plus the `update` command added by this pro"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"ject (see Updating)."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Updating"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`dsh update` moves the dsh version and re-applies the Android patches (needs `git`\non the device — `"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"pkg install git`). The patch set itself ships with this project's\nreleases, not npm; every update re"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"freshes it automatically when a newer release\nexists. `--self` is the patches-only path: it refreshe"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"s the updater + patch set\nfrom the latest release and applies them to the installed dsh directly, wi"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"thout\ndownloading a new npm package."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Flag | Effect |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| `-t, --tag TAG` | install a dist-tag directly (e.g. `next`), no version menu |\n| `-v, --version VE"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"R` | install an exact version directly (e.g. `0.1.1-rc.2`), no version menu |\n| `-y, --yes` | auto-a"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ccept every prompt |\n| `--self` | refresh the updater + patch set from the latest release and apply "},{"id":"p22s4","text":"it to the installed dsh (no npm update; `-t`/`-v` are ignored) |\n| `--patch-set PATH` | use a local "},{"id":"p22s5","text":"patch set (a directory or `.tar.gz` with `scripts/` + `patches/` + `VERSION`) instead of downloading"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"; implies `--self` and works offline |\n| `--force` | with `--self`/`--patch-set`: re-apply even when"},{"id":"p22s7","text":" the machinery is already current |\n| (no `-t`/`-v`) | interactive version menu, Enter defaults to `"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"inery is already current |\n| (no `-t`/`-v`) | interactive version menu, Enter defaults to `latest` |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"`dsh update` never restarts a running `dsh web` — start it again yourself afterwards."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## What installation changes — and how to uninstall"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Installation touches exactly three places: it unpacks the self-contained runtime (Node + patched dsh"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" + updater) into `~/.local/opt/dsh-termux-runtime/`, symlinks the `dsh` command at `~/.local/bin/dsh"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"`, and appends one PATH line tagged `# dsh-termux` at the end of `~/.bashrc`. dsh's own data (config"},{"id":"p25s4","text":", sessions) is separate, under `~/.dsh/`."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Uninstall — remove the files:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The line tagged `# dsh-termux` in `~/.bashrc` must be deleted manually."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## FAQ"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"**`dsh web` doesn't open the browser?**\nMost common cause: Termux was in the background — Android 10"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"+ silently drops activity launches from background apps. Keep Termux in the foreground, or open the "},{"id":"p30s3","text":"printed URL manually. Background details: Fix 3."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"**Update stopped with \"Patch does not apply / version drift\"?**\nA newly published dsh changed the pa"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"tched files. This is the intended safety stop — dsh stays installed but unpatched, so session saves "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"and the write tool may fail with `EACCES` on Android. File an issue or regenerate the patches per PA"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"rite tool may fail with `EACCES` on Android. File an issue or regenerate the patches per PATCHES.md."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"**`dsh update` unknown on a long-overdue install?**\nRuntimes from releases before 1.1.0 have no wrap"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"per shortcut: run the bundled updater directly — `bash ~/.local/opt/dsh-termux-runtime/scripts/updat"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"e-dsh.sh -t next -y`. From 1.1.0+ the `dsh update` shortcut keeps itself current; runtimes from befo"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"re 1.2.1 also lack the automatic patch-set refresh (updates proceed on the old set, with a notice), "},{"id":"p32s5","text":"and a fresh Option A install brings them fully current."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"**Where is my data?**\ndsh data lives in `~/.dsh/` (upstream default); this project's runtime in `~/."},{"id":"p33s2","text":"local/opt/dsh-termux-runtime/`."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Contributing"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Issues and PRs are welcome. The contributor workflow — testing gates (sandbox + on-device), CI, rele"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ases, and the update mechanism internals — is in CONTRIBUTING.md; how every Android fix works and ho"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"w to regenerate drifted patches is in PATCHES.md. If you develop with AI agents, AGENTS.md is the re"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"po protocol they follow."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Project layout"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"> Runtime artifacts (`node/`, `work/`, `downloads/`) are built outside this repository, under `~/.lo"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"cal/opt/dsh-termux-runtime/`."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## Availability statement"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
